kwbackup (0.0.15) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat(packaging): debian package, MIT license and Makefile

    debian/ installs the single-file build to /usr/bin/kwbackup and ships
    /etc/kwbackup/defaults.yaml as a conffile. debian/rules builds the artifact
    with the version from debian/changelog and runs the e2e tests.

    debian/changelog is generated from the commit history by
    packaging/gen-changelog.py (one entry per commit version) and tracked, so the
    distribution field can be edited per release.

    make build produces dist/kwbackup and the .deb; make check-version guards
    against a commit subject that disagrees with the changelog.

    LICENSE: MIT.

 -- Karel Wintersky <karel.wintersky@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:57:42 +0300

kwbackup (0.0.14) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat(build): take the version from the commit message

    build.py replaces VERSION = "LOCALDEV" in src/00_header.py with the first
    line of the current commit message; --version and KWBACKUP_VERSION override
    it. The artifact shebang is now #!/usr/bin/python3 -B and the header sets
    sys.dont_write_bytecode, so the tool never leaves __pycache__ next to itself.

    tests: build with an explicit version, --version output and shebang (19/19).

 -- Karel Wintersky <karel.wintersky@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:56:02 +0300

kwbackup (0.0.13) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat(config): built-in defaults and a single system defaults path

    Three layers: BUILTIN_DEFAULTS in src/05_builtin_defaults.py, then
    /etc/kwbackup/defaults.yaml, then the task file. The system path is the only
    one searched: the script-dir and config-dir candidates are gone, the old
    kwbackup_defaults.yaml name is gone.

    All default values now live in one dict: dataclass field defaults and parser
    fallbacks read from it instead of repeating literals in two places.

    --defaults is hidden from --help (tests and examples in place only).
    --check-config reports which layer supplied the defaults.

    tests: builtin-only scenario, defaults layer through the hidden flag, all
    examples validated against examples/defaults.yaml (18/18).

