kwbackup (0.0.10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * fix(config): do not flag rclone.conf, account-level keys are normal

    Keys inside rclone.conf mean credentials issued for the account, which is a
    supported setup; rclone flags in rclone.args override them per bucket. The
    permission check now only covers files that pass keys as flags: the task
    config and the defaults file. Documentation states the precedence explicitly.
    tests: task 0644 warns, rclone.conf with keys does not.

 -- Karel Wintersky <karel.wintersky@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:09:04 +0300

kwbackup (0.0.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat(config): make the credentials permission check configurable

    security.check_excessive_access_rights (default on) controls the warning
    about files carrying S3 keys. The check now also covers rclone.config when
    it stores access_key_id/secret_access_key, and only flags the file that
    actually carries them. Off switch lives in kwbackup_defaults.yaml for the
    whole host; --check-config prints the current state.
    tests: rclone.conf case, off switch, 17/17.

