kwbackup (0.0.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat(config): layered defaults file and per-bucket S3 keys

    kwbackup_defaults.yaml is looked up next to the script, next to the task
    config, then /etc/kwbackup (--defaults overrides). Maps merge recursively;
    option lists (rclone.args, database.args, *_compressor_args, archive.exclude)
    append with dedupe, the rest of the lists are replaced.

    Keep the BEGET/S3 mechanism: keys are issued per bucket and rclone.conf has
    env_auth = false, so --s3-access-key-id / --s3-secret-access-key in
    rclone.args are the supported path. Documented literal keys in a 0600 file
    and ${ENV} substitution; --check-config and every run warn when the file
    with credentials is readable by group/other.

    examples: host defaults + three short task configs, full.yaml stays
    self-contained; migrate keeps keys in rclone.args with a corrected note.
    tests: defaults merge scenario, 17/17.

